147:## 1. Estimand
149:I recommend **22 independent R = 12 libraries crossed with the same 20 fresh synthetic targets**. The primary quantity is \(p_T\), the probability that a fresh candidate library passes the complete arm-(i) gate on the particular target panel \(T\), under the declared seed and build rules. The observable is \(K\), the number of the 22 libraries that pass. This directly addresses what G35-B sampled only once.
153:A **yes** means the study supports stability by that definition. A **no** means it supports a pass probability below the benchmark. **Can’t tell** means the observed count cannot distinguish the two sides at the declared evidential standard. In every case, report whether changing the library actually changed a verdict. Uniform failure and mixed verdicts answer different questions, even when both rule out stable recovery. All readings apply to this synthetic scenario, grid, objective and target panel. [Owner ruling §§3–5](/home/steven/jos-g42-astra-ro/docs/research/v1_3/2026-11-20-g41-owner-ruling.md)
