173:## 3. Independent libraries and shared targets
177:Each library gets 12 fresh process/observation pairs in four predetermined batches of three. Allocate both seed streams independently of outcomes under one documented pseudorandom allocation rule. Use disjoint seed pools across libraries, targets, roles and earlier campaigns, including retired probes and reserves. I would leave the rejected G41 seed series unused for unambiguous lineage. Within a replicate, preserve the matched network/outbreak seed, fixed candidate observation namespace across cells, latent reuse across detection pairs, and frozen summation order. Reusing the process seed while changing only the observation seed would miss part of the variation of interest.
