207:I would use one fixed campaign. G35-B’s four threshold-equality counts and 0/10 batch agreement motivate measuring this variation. They do not establish its rate at R = 12. The exploratory Phase-0b diagnostic also found both offsets that moved under replicate deletion and boundary choices that persisted. A mixed B2 result could establish draw sensitivity while leaving the underlying timing–detection tradeoff unresolved. If Steven needs a claim that generalizes to *another target panel*, he should commission replication over panels as a separate estimand. G34 remains STOPPED. [Confirmed exit audit, O5](/home/steven/jos-g42-astra-ro/docs/audits/2026-11-19-g35b-campaign-exit-audit-opus-CONFIRMED.md) · [Exploratory ridge diagnostic, Q3–Q5](/home/steven/jos-g42-astra-ro/docs/research/v1_3/2026-09-29-phase0b-ridge-diagnostic-EXPLORATORY.md)
209:## 7. Compute and work caps
221:**EXPLORATORY planning estimate.** G35-B’s roughly 14½ minutes for arm (i) bought **nine** incremental candidates because B had already supplied three candidates and the targets. Scaling its candidate work by \(22\times12/9\) gives roughly **seven hours serial**. That is an order-of-magnitude estimate. Scoring more targets, retention, host I/O, sealing and independent audit have different costs. The old harness also hard-codes ten target seeds and requires a completed B generation. Budget for a numerical declaration/evaluator unit and a generation/retention unit, independent implementation review, Steven’s merge and campaign decisions, and an independent exit audit. [Campaign timing disclosures](/home/steven/jos-g42-astra-ro/docs/runs/2026-10-23-g35b-campaign-summary.json) · [Existing evaluator](/home/steven/jos-g42-astra-ro/src/jersey_outbreak/g35b_design_study.py:481)
