**A1. §§2, 7.5 and 7.6 — design rationale.** Delete §2’s `EXPECTATION` paragraph. Replace §7.5’s numbered arguments 1–5 with: “The study records whether the verdict changed among the six declared library draws on this panel. A reliability decision would require a separately commissioned standard and error budget. The six verdicts, predicate vectors and target-by-library matrices are published for a later Steven decision.” Keep the hypothetical table and its conditional interpretation. Delete the bullets beginning “For comparison with the rival proposals’ 5% convention only” and “No affordable L”. In §15, replace the corresponding affordability claim with “The pass probability on this panel remains unknown.” Delete §7.6’s `Structural floor` paragraph and the alternatives after “The 0.055 is a precedent, not a law.” Label the derived binomial and unanimity illustrations in §§7.5–7.7 `EXPLORATORY DESIGN ARITHMETIC`.

**A2. §7.7 — panel rationale.** Replace its two bullets under “What N controls” with: “At N = 20 each target contributes five percentage points to a count fraction, compared with ten at N = 10. One target can still flip a verdict at an endpoint. Twenty doubles the G35-B panel, following the earlier 5-to-10 design precedent, and preserves exact integer cutoffs.” Keep the table. Replace the sentence claiming the change cannot make any PASS easier with: “The table describes single count predicates under hypothetical per-target rates. The operating characteristics of the composite gate are unknown.” Delete the sentence offering N = 30 as an owner option and the final paragraph of §19 offering alternative L or N.

**A3. §§7.3–7.4, 7.11, 10, 12 and 13 — precedence and status.** Apply this rule throughout: “A campaign exception, an established departure from the declaration, or any false P1, P9 or P10 component makes the campaign VOID. A VOID campaign has no library verdict lines, counts `k`, `k′`, `m`, or `m_ℓ`, class, or reading. Seal the available evidence. For an intact campaign, any false P2 or P3 produces NO-READING, with cause `shared_panel` and all failed target conditions listed. All six gates are FAIL in that case. Report `k = 0` and the descriptive `k′`, `m`, and `m_ℓ`. Otherwise classify by `k`: six CONSISTENT-PASS, one through five MIXED, zero CONSISTENT-FAIL.” Remove the `library_integrity` NO-READING cause and update §13’s partition cases accordingly. Replace §7.3’s threshold boundary sentence with “Equality meets the applicable count predicate. A library passes only when all ten predicates are met.” In §7.11 use the six-token format for an intact campaign with `<PASS|FAIL>` in each slot, and append only `; G43: VOID` to the historical phrase for a VOID campaign. In §10 a VOID exit audit writes the audit verdict and cause, with no library or reading lines. In §12 replace the reviewer/defect rule with: “A step-4 defect blocks progression until corrected and independently reviewed. An established campaign defect makes the campaign VOID. DISCREPANCY denotes unresolved verification without an established departure. An intact campaign’s tokens become final only on CONFIRMED. No campaign retry or resume is allowed. A corrected rerun after VOID requires Steven’s explicit chat decision and a new owner-ruled text, using the same frozen seeds.”

