## Pre-freeze conditions

1. **Ruling commit first.** File this ruling verbatim on `main` via `fm.sh sync` with `[skip ci]`, and record the commit and committed-bytes SHA-256 through `fm.sh log`. No pre-freeze action starts before that commit exists on `main`.
2. **Pre-check on that commit.** Attest an empty diff against `0c9c3711b4e1be3fa90e9ef7f1e8e883dbdb48d8` for `src configs tests scripts`. Check and log host free space of at least 5 GB. Build all 138 §19 process seeds once in `ci` mode. Record build outcome, exception class, both fallback disclosures, and M2/M3/M4 logical hashes. Apply A7 and file the run-unique script, record and log. This step is builds-only and outcome-blind. Pool exhaustion returns the draft to the owner.
3. **Mechanical freeze.** Apply A1–A10, mark the text FROZEN, and fill the lineage and §8 placeholders from the filed evidence. Commit via `fm.sh sync` with `[skip ci]`, hash committed bytes and record the freeze commit and digest in the trail. U1 pins the digest in the config and an independent constant. A later inconsistency stops work pending a filed clarification under §12.

